    "before": {
      "attributes": {
        "id": "j174",
        "title": "T40:  a new site is three files, as jarvis-new is laid out:  `MySite.site.spell` (its routing alone, `my site is a site` with a Home at \"/\"), `main.page-layout.spell` (Star Wars' layout:  the app menu with the drawer's button and breadcrumbs) and `home.spell` (`\"Home\" is a page`, a large header).  A starter of STARTER_PROGRAMS, `site`, with an `alongside` list of the files made after the first;  SpellProjectRoot.createApp() takes a starter key as well as a file, so one createApp makes every kind.",
        "status": "open",
        "state": "open",
        "changed": "2026-11-16T12:58:24-05:00",
        "calm": ""
      },
      "label": null
    },
    "after": {
